            <ArticleTitle>Enteric group 15 (Enterobacteriaceae) associated with pneumonia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>596-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A gram-negative, oxidase-negative, fermentative rod belonging to enteric group 15 of Enterobacteriaceae was isolated in mixed culture from two patients with pneumonia. Both were elderly patients with chronic heart disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
